# Blade & frontend assets

## Views

- Calculator UI lives in `resources/views/calculate.blade.php` with logic-free partials under `partials/` and reusable `x-input-field`.
- Escape output by default (`{{ }}`). Only use `{!! !!}` when the value is trusted and intentionally HTML.
- Prefer `@include` / components over duplicating receipt, personality, or tooltip markup.
- Keep one job per section: form plan vs results receipts vs disclaimer. Do not restyle the hero into a dashboard of cards unless the design system already uses that pattern.
- When changing user-visible copy (headings, mode labels, empty states), update `tests/Feature/CalculateTest.php` in the same PR.

## CSS

- Primary styles today: `public/css/style.css` with CSS variables (`:root`). Extend that file for calculator visuals unless migrating fully to Vite.
- Prefer existing design tokens (Sora / IBM Plex, ocean palette variables) — do not introduce Inter/Roboto/Arial or purple-on-white AI-default themes.
- Avoid new card chrome (border + shadow + radius stacks) unless it wraps a real interactive control (e.g. mode radio).
- Mobile: keep the first viewport readable; mode options and receipts must remain usable on narrow screens.

## JS & Vite

- Vite is scaffolded (`resources/js/app.js`, empty `resources/css/app.css`) but the calculator currently uses static CSS + an inline mode-sync script.
- New interactive behavior: extract to `resources/js/` and load via `@vite` **or** a small deferred script partial — do not grow large inline `<script>` blocks in Blade.
- If migrating styles to Vite, move tokens from `public/css/style.css` carefully and keep `asset('css/style.css')` working until cutover is complete.
- No secrets in frontend code; only `VITE_*` public env vars if needed.

## Good vs bad

```blade
{{-- Good --}}
@include('partials.results-panel')
<a href="{{ route('calculate.show') }}">Plan</a>

{{-- Bad --}}
{!! $userProvidedHtml !!}
<a href="/calculate">Plan</a>
```
